; rdqm_drbd_helper - let DRBD's kernel-launched helpers run IBM MQ RDQM's handler on
; RHEL 10 with SELinux enforcing (#1486, epic .github#315).
;
; Generic: it names only IBM's own handler binary and stock RHEL policy types. It carries no
; site, queue manager or path specific to this lab, so it is offered upstream as a fix
; (.github#337).
;
; The defect. RDQM hooks DRBD's handlers (before/after-resync-source/target, disconnected,
; quorum-lost) as /var/mqm/rdqm/<hook> -> /opt/mqm/bin/rdqmhandler. DRBD runs them through
; the kernel's usermode helper: the kernel (kernel_t) executes drbdadm, drbdadm runs the
; handler through /bin/sh. RHEL 10's policy (selinux-policy 42.x) confines that chain. The
; kernel may not execute drbdadm or sh in place, and bin_t programs it runs land in the
; confined kernel_generic_helper_t, where rdqmhandler (systemctl, cibadmin, /var/mqm, ...)
; is denied. So every handler exits 255, RDQM never records its initial synchronization
; (DR "Waiting for initial connection", rdqmadm -s refused with AMQ6526E), and a handler
; blocked part-way can hang and wedge DRBD. RHEL 9 with the same enforcing policy and the
; same drbd-selinux 9.33.1 runs it fine.
;
; The fix:
; - the kernel may run drbdadm and its /bin/sh in place, as on RHEL 9;
; - rdqmhandler gets its own entrypoint type, and executing it from that chain transitions
;   into unconfined_service_t, the stock domain for unconfined vendor services.
; Only IBM's handler leaves confinement. Every other kernel helper stays confined.
;
; Proven under full enforcing on a 3+3 RDQM HA/DR stack (RHEL 10.2, MQ 10.0.1.0): every
; handler exits 0, HA failover and DR cutover/failback work, and no AVC is logged.
;
; Install: semodule -i rdqm_drbd_helper.cil && restorecon -v /opt/mqm/bin/rdqmhandler

(type rdqm_handler_exec_t)
(roletype object_r rdqm_handler_exec_t)
(typeattributeset file_type (rdqm_handler_exec_t))
(typeattributeset exec_type (rdqm_handler_exec_t))

(filecon "/opt/mqm/bin/rdqmhandler" file (system_u object_r rdqm_handler_exec_t ((s0) (s0))))

; The kernel's usermode helper runs drbdadm, and drbdadm's /bin/sh, in place.
(allow kernel_t drbd_exec_t (file (getattr open read map execute execute_no_trans)))
(allow kernel_t shell_exec_t (file (getattr open read map execute execute_no_trans)))

; Executing IBM's handler from that chain enters unconfined_service_t.
(allow kernel_t rdqm_handler_exec_t (file (getattr open read map execute)))
(allow kernel_t unconfined_service_t (process (transition)))
(allow unconfined_service_t rdqm_handler_exec_t (file (getattr open read map execute entrypoint)))
(typetransition kernel_t rdqm_handler_exec_t process unconfined_service_t)
(allow unconfined_service_t kernel_t (process (sigchld)))
(allow unconfined_service_t kernel_t (fd (use)))
